### =========================================================================
### CST8917 - Assignment 2 - Version B (Logic Apps + Service Bus)
### Test suite for the validation/ingestion Function endpoint.
###
### IMPORTANT: unlike Version A, the manager-approval and timeout logic runs
### inside the Logic App (see ../logic-app-workflow.json), not in this HTTP
### API. A plain HTTP client cannot drive that part directly - after queuing
### a message here, verify the rest of the flow using the Azure Portal:
###   1. Service Bus Explorer on the 'incoming-expenses' queue
###      -> peek the message the Function just sent.
###   2. Logic App > Overview > Run History
###      -> watch the run: Parse_expense_JSON -> Amount_under_$100 branch.
###   3. For amount >= $100: check the manager's inbox for the Approve/Reject
###      email (Office 365 Outlook "Send approval email" connector), or wait
###      out the PT5M demo timeout to see the escalated path fire.
###   4. Service Bus Explorer on the 'expense-outcomes' topic
###      -> peek each subscription (approved-subscription,
###      rejected-subscription, escalated-subscription) for the final
###      outcome message.
###   5. Function App logs (Application Insights Live Metrics, or the
###      `func start` console) -> notify_approved / notify_rejected /
###      notify_escalated log line: "[NOTIFICATION -> ...]".
###
### Requires the VS Code "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client).
### Start the Functions host first:  func start
### Provisioning commands for the Service Bus namespace/queue/topic are in
### ./servicebus-config.json under "provisioning.commands".
### =========================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:7071/api

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### SCENARIO 1: Valid expense < $100
### Expected: 202 Accepted here. Logic App auto-approves (no email sent);
### 'approved-subscription' should receive the outcome message.
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{baseUrl}}/expenses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "employee_name": "Alice Smith",
  "employee_email": "alice.smith@example.com",
  "amount": 45.00,
  "category": "meals",
  "description": "Team lunch with client",
  "manager_email": "manager.bob@example.com"
}


### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### SCENARIO 2: Valid expense >= $100 -> manager approves via email
### Expected: 202 Accepted here. Logic App sends an approval email to
### manager_email; click "Approve" in the email within the timeout window.
### 'approved-subscription' should receive the outcome message.
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{baseUrl}}/expenses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "employee_name": "Carlos Diaz",
  "employee_email": "carlos.diaz@example.com",
  "amount": 450.00,
  "category": "travel",
  "description": "Flight to client site in Toronto",
  "manager_email": "manager.bob@example.com"
}


### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### SCENARIO 3: Valid expense >= $100 -> manager rejects via email
### Expected: 202 Accepted here. Click "Reject" in the approval email.
### 'rejected-subscription' should receive the outcome message.
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{baseUrl}}/expenses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "employee_name": "Priya Nair",
  "employee_email": "priya.nair@example.com",
  "amount": 899.99,
  "category": "equipment",
  "description": "New graphics tablet",
  "manager_email": "manager.bob@example.com"
}


### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### SCENARIO 4: Valid expense >= $100 -> no manager response -> escalated
### Expected: 202 Accepted here. Do NOT respond to the approval email.
### After the workflow's limit.timeout (PT5M demo value) elapses,
### 'escalated-subscription' should receive the outcome message.
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{baseUrl}}/expenses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "employee_name": "Daniel Wu",
  "employee_email": "daniel.wu@example.com",
  "amount": 1200.00,
  "category": "software",
  "description": "Annual IDE license renewal",
  "manager_email": "manager.bob@example.com"
}


### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### SCENARIO 5: Missing required fields -> validation error
### Expected: 400 Bad Request directly from the Function. Nothing is queued,
### so the Logic App never runs for this request.
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{baseUrl}}/expenses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "employee_name": "Emma Brown",
  "employee_email": "emma.brown@example.com",
  "amount": 60.00,
  "category": "supplies"
}


### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### SCENARIO 6: Invalid category -> validation error
### Expected: 400 Bad Request directly from the Function. Nothing is queued.
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{baseUrl}}/expenses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "employee_name": "Frank Lee",
  "employee_email": "frank.lee@example.com",
  "amount": 250.00,
  "category": "entertainment",
  "description": "Client dinner and event tickets",
  "manager_email": "manager.bob@example.com"
}


### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### EXTRA: Malformed JSON body -> 400
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{baseUrl}}/expenses
Content-Type: application/json

{ this is not valid json }
